{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting systems. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric pure water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieves 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric pure water splitting at 420 nm",
    "Enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over nitride materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing water-splitting photocatalysts."
}

{
  "summary": "This review reassesses the pro-tumor role of M2-like tumor-associated macrophages (TAMs) by evaluating functional evidence from tumor-derived cells. It examines phagocytosis, antigen processing, cross-presentation, and CD8+ T cell activation. Findings indicate some CD206+ TAMs can cross-present tumor antigens and activate CD8+ T cells comparably to dendritic cells, correlating with improved outcomes. Counter-evidence shows macrophages may promote immunosuppression. The study emphasizes antigen fate and co-stimulatory context over M1/M2 markers for predicting function.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CD206+ tumor-associated macrophages can cross-present tumor antigens and activate CD8+ T cells at levels comparable to conventional dendritic cells",
    "These macrophages correlate with better clinical outcomes in specific contexts",
    "Antigen-presenting macrophages may retain cytotoxic T cells in tumor-promoting configurations or activate regulatory T cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes that functional capacity, not M1/M2 markers, determines macrophage immunomodulatory roles in cancer, shifting focus from surface markers to mechanistic outcomes for therapeutic targeting."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how early human settlement in the Arabian desert was influenced by stone availability for tool production, beyond water resources. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Rub' al Khali, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable materials where freshwater existed but stone was absent. Spatial analysis indicates settlement required co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, with 57% of water-accessible terrain lacking suitable stone. This challenges models that prioritize water alone, suggesting raw-material geology critically constrains dispersal.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials were found in 55 of 125 surveyed localities despite abundant freshwater",
    "Spatial modeling shows 57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, reducing false positives in site identification",
    "Convergent patterns across Africa, North America, and Asia indicate stone availability as a universal constraint on early human dispersal"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic resource availability, not water alone, was a critical factor governing early human settlement patterns across multiple continents during Pleistocene dispersals."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and inflammation in the gut. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors. Deletion of PRKAR1A reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice, and human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 in inflammation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 decreases PKA inhibitors in ILC3s, promoting inflammation",
    "PRKAR1A deletion in ILC3s reduces cell numbers and increases enteric infection risk",
    "Human intestinal ILC3s express PRKAR1A, downregulated by IL-23 in inflammatory bowel disease"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3-mediated gut homeostasis and identifies IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation as a mechanism for intestinal inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how maternal and early life obesity impacts adaptive immune responses in children. Using a mouse model replicating the obesity-epidemiological link, researchers found that high-fat diet exposure during pregnancy or early postnatal life, but not adulthood, altered naive CD4+ T cell epigenetics and transcription, impairing T follicular helper cell differentiation and vaccine responses. The mechanism involved epigenetic repression of A20 (Tnfaip3).",
  "key_findings": [
    "High-fat diet during pregnancy or early postnatal life reshapes naive CD4+ T cell epigenetics and transcription",
    "Impaired T follicular helper cell differentiation and germinal center reactions in response to vaccines",
    "Epigenetic repression of A20 (Tnfaip3) drives these immune defects"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies maternal and early life obesity as critical determinants of adaptive immune function during a developmental window, providing mechanistic insights into how obesity programs immune responses that affect vaccine efficacy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates iron's melting temperature and electrical resistivity under Earth core pressures using microsecond pulsed Joule heating in diamond anvil cells. Over 300 reproducible melting measurements reveal a shallow melting curve, reaching 6 K/GPa and 4160 ± 80 K at 200 GPa. The findings suggest a relatively cold core-mantle boundary (3430 K) and low adiabatic outer core heat flow (9.8 TW), indicating thermal convection could have powered the geodynamo before inner core formation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A shallow melting curve for iron at 200 GPa, reaching 4160 ± 80 K",
    "Inferred core-mantle boundary temperature of 3430 K",
    "Low adiabatic outer core heat flow of 9.8 TW"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The research provides critical constraints on Earth's core thermal evolution, suggesting thermal convection may have driven the geodynamo prior to inner core formation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how 4f electron filling influences bonding evolution in lanthanide single-atom catalysts across the lanthanide series. Using structurally uniform catalysts, researchers identified dual-periodic trends in binding energies, increasing from La to Eu and Gd to Yb. The findings attribute this behavior to electron redistribution between 5d and 4f orbitals, with a sharp transition at the half-filled 4f7 configuration between Eu and Gd. These results establish a 4f-electron-regulated framework for understanding lanthanide reactivity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dual-periodic trends in lanthanide-support binding energies increase from La to Eu and Gd to Yb",
    "Half-filled 4f7 configuration causes an abrupt transition between Eu and Gd",
    "Electron redistribution between 5d and 4f orbitals modulates bonding energies across diverse coordination environments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides a fundamental electronic framework for predicting and designing lanthanide-based catalysts through 4f-electron regulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated regulatory T-cell dynamics in cirrhotic HCV genotype 4 patients during and after direct-acting antiviral therapy. Using longitudinal blood sampling and flow cytometry, researchers assessed T-cell subsets at baseline, treatment, and 1 year post-viral clearance. Results showed baseline immune dysregulation with reduced T cells, increased T-cell exhaustion, and expanded Tregs and TH17 cells. After successful therapy, Tregs normalized, exhausted CD8+ T cells decreased, and immune profiles partially improved, indicating residual immune recovery post-viral clearance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Cirrhotic HCV genotype 4 patients exhibited baseline immune dysregulation with reduced CD3+ T cells and increased T-cell exhaustion markers",
    "Tregs and TH17 cells were significantly elevated at baseline compared to healthy controls",
    "Successful DAA therapy led to normalization of Tregs and reduction in exhausted CD8+ T cells within 1 year post-SVR"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study provides evidence that cirrhotic HCV patients experience distinct T-cell dysregulation that partially resolves after viral clearance, highlighting the role of immune reconstitution in chronic liver disease management."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils expressing Nlrp3 and Il1b, which license pathogenic TH17 cells. Post-recovery, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. The findings demonstrate that short-lived dietary states during specific temporal windows can durably reprogram immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates acute inflammation to chronic obesity levels in lean mice",
    "HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window blunts disease amplification",
    "Neutrophil-mediated Nlrp3-Il1b signaling licenses pathogenic TH17 cells, persisting as chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells after recovery"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that transient dietary states during narrow temporal windows can durably reprogram immune memory, revealing a mechanism by which short-lived physiological changes influence long-term inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study quantifies the global carbon sink evolution using atmospheric O2 and CO2 data from 1990 to 2019. It reveals a strengthening ocean carbon sink increasing by 2.8 ± 0.4 Pg C year-1, accounting for 35% of fossil emissions, while the net land sink shows no significant trend despite high variability. These findings challenge model simulations of land and ocean carbon sinks, suggesting current models may underestimate future climate impacts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The ocean carbon sink strengthened by 2.8 ± 0.4 Pg C year-1 between 1990 and 2019, absorbing 35% of fossil emissions.",
    "The net land carbon sink exhibited no robust trend, with a mean of 1.0 ± 0.5 Pg C year-1, accounting for 13% of fossil emissions.",
    "Model simulations of land and ocean sinks are inconsistent with observed data, potentially underestimating future climate impacts."
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides critical observational evidence of evolving carbon sinks, highlighting the ocean's increasing role in mitigating emissions and questioning the accuracy of current climate models in predicting sink dynamics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates dual sympathetic and parasympathetic nerve modulation to combat postoperative prostate cancer progression. Using personalized nanotechnology-enabled dual neurotherapy (ADNT), the researchers codelivered a β-blocker and muscarinic receptor antagonist via hybrid nanovesicles in murine models. ADNT delayed recurrence and metastasis, reduced autonomic nerve infiltration, remodeled neuro-immune crosstalk and chemokine networks, alleviated cachexia and anxiety, and achieved complete responses when combined with immune checkpoint blockade.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ADNT delayed postoperative recurrence and metastasis in refractory prostate cancer models",
    "ADNT reduced autonomic nerve infiltration and remodeled neuro-immune crosstalk and chemokine networks",
    "ADNT alleviated cancer-associated cachexia and anxiety, and induced complete responses with immune checkpoint blockade"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach demonstrates a novel dual neuromodulation strategy that effectively remodels neuro-immune interactions and chemokine signaling to suppress prostate cancer progression, offering a promising therapeutic avenue."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates γδ T cell-based immunotherapy for high-risk neuroblastoma, addressing MHC-independent recognition challenges. It evaluates γδ T cells' ability to target tumors via stress ligands and phosphoantigens, bypassing MHC class I downregulation. The research assesses γδ T cell platforms, including allogeneic products and composite therapies, to overcome immune resistance mechanisms in neuroblastoma's tumor microenvironment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "γδ T cells recognize neuroblastoma targets without MHC class I presentation",
    "Allogeneic γδ T cells show compatibility with neuroblastoma's immune microenvironment",
    "Non-engineered γ:δ T cell platforms may overcome antigen heterogeneity and immunosuppression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes γδ T cells as a promising strategy to bypass MHC class I limitations in neuroblastoma immunotherapy, potentially improving outcomes for high-risk patients."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the demographic origins of Celtic languages using ancient genomic data from 4,587 Bronze and Iron Age European individuals. By analyzing genome-wide data, the researchers identified three key population movements: Steppe-related ancestry arriving via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP, a Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain, and a westward expansion from eastern central Europe linked to Knovíz-Urnfield populations between 3200-2800 BP. The findings suggest that Celtic language spread most plausibly followed the eastern central European migration route, aligning with Iron Age Hallstatt and La Tène cultural contexts.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Steppe-related ancestry entered Europe via Bell Beaker-associated groups approximately 4400 years ago",
    "Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain occurred between 3800-3200 BP",
    "Celtic language spread likely followed a westward expansion from eastern central Europe (3200-2800 BP) linked to Knovíz-Urnfield populations"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research provides genomic evidence supporting a specific demographic pathway for Celtic language dispersal across prehistoric Europe, resolving debates about the origins and spread of Celtic languages through ancient population movements."
}

{
  "summary": "This study identifies TMEM184 family proteins as lysosomal Ca2+ uptake transporters (LyCaTs) using genetic screening. The research demonstrates TMEM184B/C selectively transport Ca2+ while excluding monovalent cations. Loss of these proteins depleted lysosomal Ca2+ stores, impaired Ca2+ release, and disrupted lysosomal exocytosis, biogenesis, and membrane repair, phenocopying TRPML1 deficiency. These findings establish TMEM184 as critical for lysosomal Ca2+ homeostasis.",
  "key_findings": [
    "TMEM184B/C proteins selectively transport Ca2+ while excluding monovalent cations",
    "Loss of TMEM184B/C depleted lysosomal Ca2+ stores and disrupted lysosomal exocytosis, biogenesis, and membrane repair",
    "A human TMEM184B mutation linked to neurodevelopmental disorders impaired lysosomal Ca2+ transport"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study identifies TMEM184 family proteins as the long-sought lysosomal Ca2+ uptake transporters essential for maintaining lysosomal Ca2+ homeostasis and function."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates high-entropy doped Li-rich layered oxide nanoparticles for high-voltage cathodes. Using laser-induced carbothermal synthesis, researchers created 83.08 nm nanoparticles with enhanced lattice stability at elevated voltages. The materials achieved stable operation up to 4.8 V with ultrahigh power density (877.9 Wh kg⁻¹) and demonstrated practical feasibility in flexible batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "High-entropy doped Li-rich nanoparticles synthesized via laser-induced carbothermal method",
    "Unprecedented small particle diameter (83.0:8 nm) enabling high lattice stability at elevated voltages",
    "Stable operation up to 4.8 V with ultrahigh power density of 877.9 Wh kg⁻¹"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a strategy for designing high-voltage stable cathodes through entropy stabilization, advancing energy storage capabilities for flexible battery applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines how polysaccharide structures modulate the tumour immune microenvironment through specific pattern-recognition receptor engagement. It identifies bidirectional immunomodulatory effects, particularly TLR4-NF-κB signaling, and highlights recent evidence of immunosuppression relief including PD-L1 downregulation and myeloid-derived suppressor cell depletion. The study emphasizes translational barriers like batch heterogeneity and the need for structure-activity models to improve clinical efficacy.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Polysaccharides exhibit bidirectional immunomodulation via TLR4-NF-κB signaling, with context-dependent activating and suppressive outputs",
    "Recent evidence shows polysaccharides relieve immunosuppression through PD-L1 downregulation, myeloid-derived suppressor cell depletion, and regulatory T cell interference",
    "Translational barriers include batch heterogeneity, lack of receptor-specific genetics, and the absence of quantitative structure-activity models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes polysaccharides as structure-informed modulators of the tumour immune microenvironment, providing a mechanistic framework for enhancing immunotherapeutic efficacy through targeted receptor engagement."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates IgA's role in mucosal homeostasis and cancer suppression. Using IgA-deficient mice, researchers found increased colorectal cancer susceptibility and epithelial proliferation due to microbiota-driven antibacterial responses. IgA treatment reduced proliferation and tumor formation, with effects mediated by DMBT1, an epithelial protein that binds IgA. The findings highlight IgA's structural role in regulating epithelial cell cycling and microbiota interactions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IgA deficiency in mice increases susceptibility to endogenous colorectal cancer",
    "IgA suppresses epithelial proliferation via DMBT1-mediated mechanisms",
    "IgA's structural properties, not binding specificity, drive tumor suppression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies IgA as a critical regulator of epithelial cell cycling in response to microbiota, providing a mechanistic basis for mucosal homeostasis and cancer prevention."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how ciliary extracellular vesicles (EVs) are formed, focusing on cargo selection and budding mechanisms. Using mouse kidney cells, researchers discovered that ESCRT-0 complexes cluster ubiquitinated Smoothened (SMO) at the ciliary tip to drive EV biogenesis without ESCRT-III machinery. Disrupting ESCRT-0 blocked SMO secretion, while forced recruitment and clustering reconstituted EV budding. These findings reveal a minimal ESCRT-0-dependent mechanism for reverse-topology EV budding.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ESCRT-0 clusters ubiquitinated SMO at the ciliary tip to drive EV biogenesis",
    "SMO secretion requires ESCRT-0 condensation but not ESCRT-III machinery",
    "Forced ESCRT-0 recruitment and SMO clustering reconstitute EV budding"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies ESCRT-0 condensation and cargo clustering as a minimal mechanism for ESCRT-III-independent reverse-topology extracellular vesicle budding from cilia."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses selective ammonium recovery from wastewater using capacitive deionization (CDI). Researchers engineered an organic material, IPB, with extended electron delocalization and C═N groups to enhance NH4+ adsorption while maintaining selectivity. The IPB-based CDI achieved high capacity (267.23 mg g-1), fast kinetics (62.51 mg g-1 min-1), and exceptional selectivity in complex streams. It reduced NH4+ to below 3 mg L-1 and achieved 82.3% fertilizer recovery with a low carbon footprint of 4.66 × 10-2 t CO2-eq per tonne treated.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IPB-based CDI achieved 267.23 mg g-1 NH4+ adsorption capacity",
    "The system maintained high selectivity in multi-ion matrices with fast kinetics (62.51 mg g-1 min-1)",
    "CDI reduced NH4+ to <3 mg L-1 and achieved 82.3% fertilizer recovery with low carbon footprint (4.66 × 10-2 t CO2-eq per tonne)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This molecular engineering approach overcomes the capacity-selectivity trade-off in CDI, enabling sustainable ammonium recovery from wastewater with minimal environmental impact."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated paeoniflorin's (PF) mechanism in systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) by assessing its impact on gut microbiota, lysophospholipid metabolism, and Th17/Treg balance. Using MRL/lpr mice, PF reduced autoantibodies, improved renal function, and restored immune homeostasis by suppressing lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) and lysophosphatidylcholine (LPC) production, thereby modulating gut microbiota composition and Th17/Treg cell populations.",
  "key_findings": [
    "PF treatment reduced splenomegaly, lymphadenopathy, and autoantibodies in SLE mice",
    "PF suppressed IL-17-producing CD4⁺ T cells and promoted Foxp3⁺ Treg cells",
    "PF decreased lysophosphatidic acid (LPA) and lysophosphatidylcholine (LPC) levels, linking gut microbiota shifts to Th17/Treg balance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a gut microbiota-lipid metabolite axis as a key mechanism for paeoniflorin's immunomodulatory effects in SLE, providing a potential therapeutic target for immune dysregulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how brown adipocyte heterogeneity regulates thermogenesis. It identifies IL-1β from neutrophils and macrophages stabilizing low-UCP1-expressing adipocytes (BA-L) via glucocorticoid receptor activation. Cold exposure shifts BA-L to high-UCP1-expressing cells (BA-H), enhancing thermogenesis, while aging elevates IL-1β, locking BA-L cells and causing cold intolerance. Targeting glucocorticoid signaling reverses age-related thermogenic decline.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-1β secreted by immune cells stabilizes BA-L cells by maintaining glucocorticoid receptor activity",
    "Cold exposure converts BA-L to BA-H cells, increasing UCP1-dependent thermogenesis",
    "Aging elevates IL-1β, reducing BA-H/BA-L ratio and causing cold intolerance, reversible via glucocorticoid signaling"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a neuronal-immune mechanism controlling brown adipocyte plasticity to thermogenesis, providing insights into age-related metabolic decline."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the composition and formation conditions of icy grains in β Pictoris' debris disk using JWST near-infrared spectroscopy. The analysis revealed amorphous water ice with low crystallinity and carbon dioxide ice in both 12CO2 and 13CO. The ices are mixed at a 1:10 ratio, suggesting cold interstellar origin and frequent collisions maintaining uniform distribution.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Amorphous water ice with <7% crystallinity detected in the debris disk",
    "Carbon dioxide ice observed in both 12CO2 and 13CO2 isotopologues",
    "CO2 ice mixed with water ice at a 1:10 ratio indicating cold interstellar origin"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that icy grains in debris disks can form in cold interstellar environments and remain mixed through frequent collisions, providing insights into the early stages of planetary system evolution."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing sulfur utilization in all-solid-state lithium-sulfur batteries by addressing unbalanced carrier transport dynamics. The researchers developed surface-bound ion-electron convergent interphases using Li2FeS2 on Li2S to bridge separated ion and electron pathways. The approach reduced transport tortuosity and activation barriers, enabling stable cycling over 10,000 cycles with 97.8% sulfur utilization at 1 mg cm-2 and a record areal capacity of 38.69 mAh cm-2.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Surface-bound Li2FeS2 interphases bridge ion and electron pathways at Li2S surfaces",
    "97.8% sulfur utilization at 1 mg cm-2 with stable cycling over 10,000 cycles",
    "Record areal capacity of 38.69 mAh cm-2 achieved through reduced transport tortuosity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a design principle for synchronizing ion-electron transfer in all-solid-state batteries by creating surface-bound interphases that overcome transport limitations in sulfur-based systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated dual-targeted thalidomide nanoliposomes for suppressing neutrophil-driven inflammation in intestinal Behçet's disease. The researchers designed nanoliposomes co-functionalized with neutrophil elastase-binding and P-selectin-binding peptides to enhance targeted delivery. In vivo results showed improved intestinal retention, reduced neutrophil infiltration, and alleviated tissue injury in a murine model, indicating enhanced efficacy over conventional therapies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Thd-NEBP/PSN-Lip demonstrated 2.6-fold higher intestinal retention than Thd-Lip at 24 hours in vivo",
    "The dual-ligand nanoliposomes reduced neutrophil infiltration and inflammatory cytokines while restoring regulatory T cells in intestinal tissue",
    "In vitro validation confirmed enhanced ligand-dependent interactions with activated endothelial cells and platelets"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a targeted delivery strategy for immunomodulatory therapeutics in inflammatory bowel diseases by engaging specific neutrophil and platelet inflammatory interfaces."
}
